{
  "playedAs": "Rook",
  "transcript": [
    "A heavy door, banded in iron, set into the living rock. There is a keyhole in it the size of a thumb, and daylight under the sill.\n\nThere is a passage to the south.\n\nYou've found the exit! The key you are carrying fits this lock. Open it and you are out \u2014 alive, which almost nothing here manages, and not coming back. Whatever you are carrying goes with you; whatever you have left undone stays undone.",
    "> open the door",
    "The key turns over hard, and the door gives.\n\nBeyond it is daylight, and cold air, and country this world does not know the shape of. You walk out into it carrying dagger, key, shortsword, leather armor, after 40 minutes underground.\n\nThat is the end of Rook \u2014 the only ending here that is not dying. Almost everything that has ever left this place left it on its back. You did not.",
    "Name your next character."
  ],
  "note": "What you did there is in the world's record like anyone else's, and anyone present saw it."
}
